body:
I tinkered a bit, looks like with [C++20](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100749) it will be possible in a pretty minimalistic way:

```c++
template <typename T, typename U>
concept exact_type_t = std::is_same_v<T, U>;

int add(exact_type_t<int> auto p_lhs, exact_type_t<int> auto p_rhs) {
    return p_lhs + p_rhs;
}

int main() {
    std::cout << add(2, 3); // Works
    std::cout << add(2l, 3); // Static error
    return 0;
}
```

It's especially nice how no `template` is needed. The only thing I dislike is needing the 'auto' but I suppose that's just how it is.

Edit: Actually, this exact concept is a [core C++20 feature](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/concepts/same_as) apparently, so we don't even need our own concept:

```c++
int add(std::same_as<int> auto p_lhs, std::same_as<int> auto p_rhs) {
    return p_lhs + p_rhs;
}

int main() {
    std::cout << add(2, 3); // Works
    std::cout << add(2l, 3); // Static error
    return 0;
}
```
